.TH FOREST-LOCKSCREEN 1 "October 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-lockscreen \- Forest lock screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-lockscreen
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-lockscreen
locks the session through the Wayland
.I ext-session-lock-v1
protocol, asks for the user's password (PAM service
.IR forest-locker ),
unlocks and exits. It prints
.B locked
on standard output once the compositor confirms the screen is covered.
It is styled with the active Forest theme's
.IR greeter.css .
.PP
It is normally started by
.BR forest-locker (1)
rather than by hand.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Unlock without authenticating.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after unlocking; non-zero if the session couldn't be locked (for
example, another locker already holds the lock).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest-locker (1)
